mpc2000xl: open the sampling input at machine start

MAME opens the OSD capture node when the emulated machine first reads its
input stream, so the MPC sampling input only appeared in the host graph
once the firmware armed recording. Read both input channels on every
stream update while the recorder is idle and discard the samples: the
input node then exists from machine start, and routing host audio into it
does not depend on arming sampling first.

--- a/src/devices/sound/l7a1045_l6028_dsp_a.cpp
+++ b/src/devices/sound/l7a1045_l6028_dsp_a.cpp
@@ -296,6 +296,8 @@
 	// plays, and a voice may be reading the very RAM recording will fill.
 	if (m_rec_on)
 		record_capture(stream);
+	else
+		warm_capture_input(stream);
 
 	for (int i = 0; i < NUM_VOICES; i++)
 	{
@@ -865,6 +867,19 @@
 	m_adc_drq_handler(want ? ASSERT_LINE : CLEAR_LINE);
 }
 
+// The OSD creates its capture node when the machine first reads its input,
+// so read both channels on every update even while the recorder is idle:
+// the host-side input stream then exists from machine start, and routing
+// audio into it does not depend on arming sampling first.
+void l7a1045_sound_device::warm_capture_input(sound_stream &stream)
+{
+	for (int j = 0; j < stream.samples(); j++)
+	{
+		for (int ch = 0; ch < 2; ch++)
+			stream.get(ch, j);
+	}
+}
